##### xbcon_rules.py (docs/bdos/CONIN.md)
  == R-BC-CONST: CONST ($0B) answers A 0 with no key waiting and A $FF with one -- and TAKES that key out of the BIOS key buffer (GETPNT moves by one) into the DOS's own one-key hold: the next input call returns it. Nothing is echoed.
     candidate fails 2 case(s); zerobas fails 2
     e.g. XN D01 a: VG 0xff | CAND 0x00 | ZB 0xff | NMS 0xff
     fields: {'ZB=VG': 2, 'ZB other': 2, 'ZB=CAND': 4} {'NMS=VG': 8}
  == R-BC-HOLD: A held key comes first. CONIN after CONST returns CONST's 'X' though 'A' was put in the BIOS buffer for it; echoing 'X', CONIN takes the waiting 'A' into the hold too (the buffer is empty after it), and DIRIO with E $FF then returns that 'A' although the BIOS buffer is empty -- not A 0.
     candidate fails 4 case(s); zerobas fails 4
     e.g. XN D02 a: VG 0x58 | CAND 0x00 | ZB 0x41 | NMS 0x58
     fields: {'ZB other': 10, 'ZB=CAND': 6, 'ZB=VG': 6} {'NMS=VG': 22}
  == R-BC-RAW: DIRIO ($06) with E $FF, $07 and $08 return the waiting key in A and take it from the buffer, with NO echo: the cursor and the screen stay.
     candidate fails 6 case(s); zerobas fails 6
     e.g. XN D04 a: VG 0x42 | CAND 0x00 | ZB 0x42 | NMS 0x42
     fields: {'ZB=VG': 20, 'ZB other': 10, 'ZB=CAND': 6} {'NMS=VG': 36}
  == R-BC-ECHO: CONIN ($01) returns the key and echoes it through the console: 'E' is written at the cursor (column 1 -> 2). Return ($0D) echoes as a carriage return ALONE: the cursor goes to column 1 of the SAME row. CTRL+A ($01) is echoed raw -- no '^A': nothing appears and the cursor stays, but it is the graphic
     candidate fails 6 case(s); zerobas fails 4
